THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

Quran.ws / Quran Stack
  Quran Engine 0.8.0 (npm dependency): Copyright 2026 Quran.ws. Code is MIT.
  Source: https://github.com/quran-ws/quran-engine
  See the package's LICENSE and LICENSES directory for the full terms, including
  the separate terms for data and third-party material.
  The reader uses QVP browser bindings and their paired renderer WASM. QVP
  v0.5.0 assets (including atlas, page vectors and surah font) have separate
  source-bundle terms: https://cdn.quran.ws/qvp/v0.5.0/
  See https://quran.ws/docs/reference/licensing and confirm the terms applicable
  to the exact renderer, data and fonts before redistribution.

Quran Lab / TajweedFormer
  The supported reader uses the vendored TajweedFormer browser client 3.1.3
  from the supplied reader, with its packaged worker, glue and WASM. The SDK
  handles model provisioning, selection and distribution; this repository
  does not bundle model weights.
  TajweedFormer 4.0.0 is a declared npm dependency and is not used by the
  supported reader. Source: https://github.com/Quran-Lab/tajweedformer-web
  Quran-Lab No-Profit License 1.2 (NPL-1.2).
  Copyright (c) 2026 Muno459 / Quran-Lab.
  The license prohibits charging for access to the covered work or features
  it powers, and presenting the work as authoritative religious judgment.
  Consult the full terms in the npm package and preserve the bundled asset
  notices at frontend/public/TAJWEEDFORMER_LICENSE.txt and
  frontend/public/RETAINED_THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

quran-json 3.1.2 — Risan Bagja
  Source: https://github.com/risan/quran-json
  License: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
  The backend fetches Uthmani verse text unchanged from the published jsDelivr
  package and normalizes text in memory for search. This source is not used as
  approved pronunciation data.

Other dependencies and assets
  FastAPI, Pydantic, Uvicorn, HTTPX, Pytest and Vite remain subject to their
  upstream licenses. See frontend/package-lock.json and backend/pyproject.toml.
  Preserve applicable notices for Quran text, pronunciation/alignment data,
  the Hafs Smart font, audio cues and other included assets. Confirm their
  terms with the applicable rights holders before redistribution.

